# Python Code Style — ATLAS Conventions

## Verbosity and Clarity

- Code reads like English. No clever one-liners.
- Every step on its own line. Variable names are long and descriptive.
- Maximum 40 lines per function. Extract named helpers if approaching 40.
- Type hints on EVERY function parameter and return value — no exceptions.
- Type checker is `pyright`. `mypy` is banned.

## Naming

- Files and variables: `snake_case` — e.g. `data_manager.py`, `signal_score`
- Classes: `PascalCase` — e.g. `LunarCrushProvider`, `SignalAggregator`
- Constants: `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` — e.g. `MAX_POSITION_SIZE`, `API_TIMEOUT`

## Function Prefix Vocabulary

Use these three prefixes consistently. They cover ~80% of all functions:

| Prefix       | Use For                              | Example                                          |
|-------------|--------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------|
| `fetch_`    | External API calls                   | `fetch_lunarcrush_sentiment(asset: str) -> SentimentData` |
| `calculate_`| Logic, math, processing — no API calls| `calculate_confluence_score(signals: list[Signal]) -> float` |
| `send_`     | Outbound actions — signals, notifications | `send_signal_to_prometheus(signal: SignalObject) -> bool` |

## Data Models

- Use Pydantic v2 `BaseModel` with `frozen=True` for all data transfer objects.
- Use `Field(description="...")` on every field.
- Use `field_validator` for cross-field validation.
- NO `dataclasses` for domain models — use Pydantic BaseModel.

## Financial Values — Decimal is Mandatory

All financial fields use `decimal.Decimal`, never `float`:
- prices, stop losses, take profits, PnL, fees, slippage, funding costs
- account equity, margin, collateral

Explicit exception: dimensionless technical indicators may use `float`:
- RSI, MACD, stochastic oscillator values
- confidence scores, probabilities, weights (0.0–1.0)

## Time-Series Data

- Use Polars `LazyFrame` for OHLCV and other time-series data.
- `pandas` is banned outright.

## Imports

- Group: stdlib → third-party → local, separated by blank lines
- Use `from __future__ import annotations` at top of every file

## Configuration

- `PolarisSettings` (pydantic-settings) is the ONLY source of config.
- `os.getenv()` and `os.environ[...]` are banned in application code.